WEBVTT

1
00:00:42.958 --> 00:00:45.958
In the previous verses of Chapter 12,

2
00:00:45.958 --> 00:00:48.041
Lord Krishna described various levels

3
00:00:48.041 --> 00:00:51.666
for progressing on the path of devotion,

4
00:00:51.666 --> 00:00:53.916
and now, in the remaining verses

5
00:00:53.916 --> 00:00:55.541
of this chapter, Lord Krishna

6
00:00:55.541 --> 00:00:59.958
describes the inner qualities of an ideal devotee.

7
00:00:59.958 --> 00:01:03.291
From these verses 12.13 and 12.14

8
00:01:03.291 --> 00:01:05.166
until the end of the chapter,

9
00:01:05.166 --> 00:01:06.291
Lord Krishna will

10
00:01:06.291 --> 00:01:08.541
describe thirty-five qualities

11
00:01:08.541 --> 00:01:10.250
that make an ideal devotee

12
00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:13.041
most dear to Lord Krishna.

13
00:01:13.041 --> 00:01:14.958
By mentioning these qualities,

14
00:01:14.958 --> 00:01:17.000
Lord Krishna is explaining to us

15
00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:20.250
how the conduct, behaviour,

16
00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:23.333
and perspective of an ideal devotee should be.

17
00:01:23.333 --> 00:01:26.458
These qualities are a source of inspiration for us,

18
00:01:26.458 --> 00:01:28.916
because by adopting all of these,

19
00:01:28.916 --> 00:01:32.041
our devotion can deepen further,

20
00:01:32.041 --> 00:01:36.583
and we too can become
most dear to Lord Krishna.

21
00:01:41.166 --> 00:01:42.958
Lord Krishna here describes many

22
00:01:42.958 --> 00:01:45.958
qualities of an ideal devotee.

23
00:01:45.958 --> 00:01:48.750
Let us understand these qualities.

24
00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:51.666
First, adveshta, meaning

25
00:01:51.666 --> 00:01:55.541
one who holds no hatred
or enmity toward anyone,

26
00:01:55.541 --> 00:01:58.583
even if someone treats them badly.

27
00:01:58.583 --> 00:02:01.708
For this devotee, good and bad

28
00:02:01.708 --> 00:02:03.416
both are parts of Lord Krishna's

29
00:02:03.416 --> 00:02:07.291
divine plan, and keeping this feeling,

30
00:02:07.291 --> 00:02:08.625
they maintain a

31
00:02:08.625 --> 00:02:11.250
friendly attitude with all.

32
00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:14.750
This is why the second quality mentioned

33
00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:17.500
is maitrah, meaning

34
00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:20.833
friendly. The third quality

35
00:02:20.833 --> 00:02:23.875
Lord Krishna explains with the word karunah,

36
00:02:23.875 --> 00:02:24.958
meaning this

37
00:02:24.958 --> 00:02:28.250
devotee has compassion and
mercy in the heart.

38
00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:31.791
And yes, this does not mean pitying someone,

39
00:02:31.791 --> 00:02:34.916
but is a genuine concern.

40
00:02:34.916 --> 00:02:36.500
Such a devotee sincerely

41
00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:38.000
wishes to remove

42
00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:39.916
others' suffering,

43
00:02:39.916 --> 00:02:41.333
because they know

44
00:02:41.333 --> 00:02:45.375
that all are suffering from
the illusions of the world.

45
00:02:45.375 --> 00:02:47.791
The next quality is nirmamah,

46
00:02:47.791 --> 00:02:48.708
meaning

47
00:02:48.708 --> 00:02:51.708
this devotee does not consider
anything as their own.

48
00:02:51.708 --> 00:02:56.541
Their conviction is that everything
belongs to Lord Krishna.

49
00:02:56.541 --> 00:03:01.250
Similarly, nirahankarah, without ego.

50
00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:04.875
This devotee never takes pride in their body,

51
00:03:04.875 --> 00:03:08.166
social status, or position

52
00:03:08.166 --> 00:03:11.500
as their identity.

53
00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:14.750
The next quality is sama-duhkha-sukhah,

54
00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:17.125
meaning whether joy or sorrow,

55
00:03:17.125 --> 00:03:19.500
they remain equal in both,

56
00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:21.375
because this devotee knows

57
00:03:21.375 --> 00:03:25.500
that both joy and sorrow are temporary.

58
00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:27.500
The next quality is kshami,

59
00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:30.208
meaning forgiving,

60
00:03:30.208 --> 00:03:32.875
because if joy and sorrow are both temporary,

61
00:03:32.875 --> 00:03:35.916
and everything is part of Lord Krishna's plan,

62
00:03:35.916 --> 00:03:38.125
then why hold resentment toward others?

63
00:03:38.125 --> 00:03:41.666
So this devotee keeps a forgiving heart.

64
00:03:41.666 --> 00:03:45.000
The next important quality is santushtah,

65
00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:48.541
meaning this devotee is always content.

66
00:03:48.541 --> 00:03:53.750
There is no constant longing
in their mind to acquire.

67
00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:56.375
Such a devotee is satatam yogi,

68
00:03:56.375 --> 00:03:58.333
an ever-present yogi,

69
00:03:58.333 --> 00:04:02.791
who remains regularly engaged
in spiritual practice.

70
00:04:02.791 --> 00:04:05.291
Yatatma is the next quality,

71
00:04:05.291 --> 00:04:09.458
which means self-control.

72
00:04:09.458 --> 00:04:12.666
Such a devotee also has dridha-nishchayah,

73
00:04:12.666 --> 00:04:15.791
meaning they remain steadfast on their path,

74
00:04:15.791 --> 00:04:19.416
and do not waver in the face of difficulties.

75
00:04:19.416 --> 00:04:20.375
And finally,

76
00:04:20.375 --> 00:04:21.833
Lord Krishna, explaining the essence

77
00:04:21.833 --> 00:04:24.916
of such a devotee's life, says,

78
00:04:24.916 --> 00:04:27.791
mayy-arpita-mano-buddhir,

79
00:04:27.791 --> 00:04:30.208
meaning a devotee who has surrendered

80
00:04:30.208 --> 00:04:31.250
both mind

81
00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:33.750
and intellect to Lord Krishna.

82
00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:36.458
They do no action out of selfishness.

83
00:04:36.458 --> 00:04:37.500
Everything is

84
00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:41.541
lovingly offered to Lord Krishna.

85
00:04:41.541 --> 00:04:43.083
And then come

86
00:04:43.083 --> 00:04:45.750
Lord Krishna's golden words,

87
00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:49.583
yo mad-bhaktah sa me priyah,

88
00:04:49.583 --> 00:04:53.625
such a devotee is most dear to Me.

89
00:04:53.625 --> 00:04:55.166
This verse explains

90
00:04:55.166 --> 00:04:58.375
that devotion is not only the
name of outer actions.

91
00:04:58.375 --> 00:05:01.583
True devotion brings inner transformation.

92
00:05:01.583 --> 00:05:03.416
True devotion means

93
00:05:03.416 --> 00:05:06.250
developing a personality

94
00:05:06.250 --> 00:05:10.375
that is free from envy, ego, and desire,

95
00:05:10.375 --> 00:05:13.375
and filled with compassion, tolerance,

96
00:05:13.375 --> 00:05:17.625
and unwavering trust in Lord Krishna.

97
00:05:22.291 --> 00:05:23.833
In this verse,

98
00:05:23.833 --> 00:05:27.291
both santushtah, contentment,

99
00:05:27.291 --> 00:05:31.083
and dridha-nishchayah,
firm resolve, are mentioned.

100
00:05:31.083 --> 00:05:32.833
Now this

101
00:05:32.833 --> 00:05:35.958
may have raised a question in many minds,

102
00:05:35.958 --> 00:05:38.208
is it possible

103
00:05:38.208 --> 00:05:41.333
to be content with life

104
00:05:41.333 --> 00:05:46.500
and yet have firm resolve to move forward?

105
00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:50.458
Because it is a common belief

106
00:05:50.458 --> 00:05:55.041
that contentment means staying where you are,

107
00:05:55.041 --> 00:05:59.666
and firm resolve means

108
00:05:59.666 --> 00:06:02.958
pressing ahead toward a goal.

109
00:06:02.958 --> 00:06:05.500
True contentment

110
00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:08.666
is not the name of stopping.

111
00:06:08.666 --> 00:06:13.333
True contentment says that you

112
00:06:13.333 --> 00:06:15.916
wish to keep growing,

113
00:06:15.916 --> 00:06:21.083
but you are also content with your present.

114
00:06:21.083 --> 00:06:24.500
You do not grieve that

115
00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:25.916
you have not

116
00:06:25.916 --> 00:06:29.333
yet reached your goal, because

117
00:06:29.333 --> 00:06:33.875
you trust that if you keep moving forward,

118
00:06:33.875 --> 00:06:36.875
the goal will be reached.

119
00:06:36.875 --> 00:06:38.625
Think about this,

120
00:06:38.625 --> 00:06:42.500
when you climb a mountain for joy,

121
00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:45.125
do you grieve at every step

122
00:06:45.125 --> 00:06:47.708
because you have not

123
00:06:47.708 --> 00:06:50.583
yet reached the summit?

124
00:06:50.583 --> 00:06:51.916
No.

125
00:06:51.916 --> 00:06:55.375
You move forward, you climb,

126
00:06:55.375 --> 00:07:00.208
and here and there you pause to enjoy nature.

127
00:07:00.208 --> 00:07:02.833
But at the same time your resolve

128
00:07:02.833 --> 00:07:06.000
is to reach the summit.

129
00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:08.375
In this, you know

130
00:07:08.375 --> 00:07:10.708
that the journey is beautiful too,

131
00:07:10.708 --> 00:07:14.208
and the goal also matters.

132
00:07:14.208 --> 00:07:16.166
This is the harmony of contentment

133
00:07:16.166 --> 00:07:19.416
and firm resolve.

134
00:07:19.416 --> 00:07:22.416
If you give up contentment,

135
00:07:22.416 --> 00:07:25.708
the mind will always be restless,

136
00:07:25.708 --> 00:07:29.666
because life's joy will always seem

137
00:07:29.666 --> 00:07:32.541
to lie in the future.

138
00:07:32.541 --> 00:07:37.166
And if you give up firm resolve,

139
00:07:37.166 --> 00:07:40.500
you will suffer staying in one place,

140
00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:42.750
watching your hidden talents

141
00:07:42.750 --> 00:07:46.166
go to waste.

142
00:07:46.166 --> 00:07:48.000
So give up neither

143
00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:52.583
contentment nor firm resolve.

144
00:07:52.583 --> 00:07:55.875
A beautiful life is one where

145
00:07:55.875 --> 00:07:59.583
you are happy with the present,

146
00:07:59.583 --> 00:08:03.750
and also making progress toward the future.

147
00:08:08.291 --> 00:08:10.041
Think about the last time

148
00:08:10.041 --> 00:08:15.208
when a family member hurt your feelings.

149
00:08:15.208 --> 00:08:19.375
Perhaps they said something harsh,

150
00:08:19.375 --> 00:08:22.583
did not see your concern and love,

151
00:08:22.583 --> 00:08:25.000
or perhaps they

152
00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:28.458
did not live up to your expectations.

153
00:08:28.458 --> 00:08:31.166
How did you feel then?

154
00:08:31.166 --> 00:08:33.958
Sorrow, anger,

155
00:08:33.958 --> 00:08:38.333
or a wound within?

156
00:08:38.333 --> 00:08:42.833
The root of this is often

157
00:08:42.833 --> 00:08:48.000
the feeling of mam, 'mine.'

158
00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:49.833
I loved them,

159
00:08:49.833 --> 00:08:52.250
then why did they not understand?

160
00:08:52.250 --> 00:08:54.666
I did so much for them,

161
00:08:54.666 --> 00:08:58.500
then why did they not listen?

162
00:08:58.500 --> 00:09:02.333
When you attach these great expectations

163
00:09:02.333 --> 00:09:06.875
to your love and duty,

164
00:09:06.875 --> 00:09:08.500
then pain

165
00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:10.333
will follow.

166
00:09:10.333 --> 00:09:11.458
But think,

167
00:09:11.458 --> 00:09:16.458
what if you fulfilled your duty with love,

168
00:09:16.458 --> 00:09:19.875
and without expecting

169
00:09:19.875 --> 00:09:23.958
a particular response from the other person?

170
00:09:23.958 --> 00:09:26.541
This is

171
00:09:26.541 --> 00:09:28.500
nirmam.

172
00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:32.333
Freedom from 'I'

173
00:09:32.333 --> 00:09:33.625
and 'mine.'

174
00:09:33.625 --> 00:09:36.791
This feeling comes from the understanding

175
00:09:36.791 --> 00:09:41.208
that everyone has their
own life and circumstances.

176
00:09:41.208 --> 00:09:44.125
Your work is to give love,

177
00:09:44.125 --> 00:09:46.375
and do your duty.

178
00:09:46.375 --> 00:09:49.458
And their life is their own.

179
00:09:49.458 --> 00:09:53.666
And when we add to this

180
00:09:53.666 --> 00:09:55.708
nirahankar,

181
00:09:55.708 --> 00:09:59.666
then anyone's words

182
00:09:59.666 --> 00:10:01.666
stop causing hurt.

183
00:10:01.666 --> 00:10:04.125
Whether praise or criticism,

184
00:10:04.125 --> 00:10:06.041
all pass without affecting you,

185
00:10:06.041 --> 00:10:09.583
coming and going like a wave.

186
00:10:09.583 --> 00:10:13.625
Only then does forgiveness become possible,

187
00:10:13.625 --> 00:10:17.125
because for the sake of your own peace,

188
00:10:17.125 --> 00:10:21.958
you release them from all blame,

189
00:10:21.958 --> 00:10:24.291
and forgive them.

190
00:10:24.291 --> 00:10:28.125
Keep love and duty.

191
00:10:28.125 --> 00:10:32.250
Reduce expectations and ego,

192
00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:35.750
and awaken a forgiving heart.

193
00:10:35.750 --> 00:10:39.708
Then watch how joyful

194
00:10:39.708 --> 00:10:41.958
family life becomes.

195
00:10:46.583 --> 00:10:50.166
When someone else at
work receives a promotion

196
00:10:50.166 --> 00:10:52.791
or greater praise,

197
00:10:52.791 --> 00:10:57.000
do you feel envy or jealousy?

198
00:10:57.000 --> 00:10:58.541
Can you genuinely

199
00:10:58.541 --> 00:11:02.916
support others' success?

200
00:11:02.916 --> 00:11:05.375
If not,

201
00:11:05.375 --> 00:11:09.750
then some changes will need to be made,

202
00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:11.708
because true progress and peace

203
00:11:11.708 --> 00:11:15.000
will come only to one

204
00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:16.708
who is adveshta,

205
00:11:16.708 --> 00:11:19.416
meaning toward others,

206
00:11:19.416 --> 00:11:23.208
free from enmity.

207
00:11:23.208 --> 00:11:25.875
Another person's progress

208
00:11:25.875 --> 00:11:27.416
does not create

209
00:11:27.416 --> 00:11:29.875
envy in such a person.

210
00:11:29.875 --> 00:11:32.833
When you begin to see others not as competitors

211
00:11:32.833 --> 00:11:35.916
but as fellow travellers,

212
00:11:35.916 --> 00:11:39.333
then this inner change has a positive effect

213
00:11:39.333 --> 00:11:42.666
on your own progress too.

214
00:11:42.666 --> 00:11:47.458
And those who hold no enmity in their hearts,

215
00:11:47.458 --> 00:11:49.583
I Myself help them.

216
00:11:49.583 --> 00:11:51.458
Also bring

217
00:11:51.458 --> 00:11:53.458
the word maitrah

218
00:11:53.458 --> 00:11:56.458
into your life too.

219
00:11:56.458 --> 00:11:59.333
Toward those who are walking alongside you,

220
00:11:59.333 --> 00:12:02.666
maintain a spirit of friendship.

221
00:12:02.666 --> 00:12:05.833
Find joy in their success,

222
00:12:05.833 --> 00:12:08.125
and instead of competition,

223
00:12:08.125 --> 00:12:10.958
create an environment of cooperation.

224
00:12:10.958 --> 00:12:14.000
Toward those who have fallen behind you,

225
00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:17.125
hold compassion.

226
00:12:17.125 --> 00:12:19.250
Help them in their progress,

227
00:12:19.250 --> 00:12:21.000
offer guidance,

228
00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:24.500
and share your knowledge with them.

229
00:12:24.500 --> 00:12:28.041
Only one who can lead for the long term

230
00:12:28.041 --> 00:12:30.708
is the one who, along with their own progress,

231
00:12:30.708 --> 00:12:33.166
also lifts others forward.

232
00:12:33.166 --> 00:12:36.291
When you work with such qualities,

233
00:12:36.291 --> 00:12:40.208
the atmosphere of the workplace itself changes.

234
00:12:40.208 --> 00:12:43.583
Instead of racing against others,

235
00:12:43.583 --> 00:12:47.250
you run together with them toward the goal.

236
00:12:47.250 --> 00:12:51.500
You help them, and they help you.

237
00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:57.083
And then you receive not
only promotion or progress,

238
00:12:57.083 --> 00:13:02.125
but something even more precious,

239
00:13:02.125 --> 00:13:03.708
which is

240
00:13:03.708 --> 00:13:07.291
the trust of others, their respect,

241
00:13:07.291 --> 00:13:10.958
and inner peace.
